/P 119 0 R
/E (Eye tracking correlates with concussion symptoms and detected convergence and accommodative abnormalities associated with concussion in the pediatric population. It demonstrates utility as a rapid, objective, noninvasive aid in the diagnosis of concussion. Eye tracking reliably detected convergence and accommodative abnormalities as well as other types of oculomotor dysfunction associated with concussion in the pediatric population. These results demonstrate the utility of eye tracking as a rapid, objective, noninvasive aid in the diagnosis of concussion that does not require pre-injury data for interpretation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
